        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk programme on cream silk in blue typography with slight fringe to sides, printed on both sides.  Produced for 'Grand Morning Performance in aid of the Masonic Charities' a variety production with the Carl Rosa Opera Company, selections of music and song, scenes from 'Monte Carlo' and 'My Neighbour's Wife', and the D'Oyly Carte Opera Company performing Act Two of 'The Mikado', Manchester Theatre Royal, 3rd April 1897."@en ;
